Subject: [PATCH 04081/11362] [outer-loop] .438 KV260 task: strip literal
 /dev/mmcblk (was blocking activation in a retry loop)

CRITICAL: .438 activation was REFUSED 6x in a row (03:25-03:36 UTC,
WRONG_MECHANISM_PRECONDITION) -- my pre-staged exp4767-c KV260 task included the
literal '/dev/mmcblk*' inside a WARNING ('host SD-card device nodes (/dev/mmcblk*)
are PERMANENTLY retired'). The exclusion_manifest_lint guard matches KV260 + /dev/mmcblk
regardless of the negative/warning context (no override path) -- the exact false-positive
that blocked .437 activation earlier (resolved the same way). Stripped the literal token;
the SSH-only precondition + 'host SD-card device nodes are permanently retired' wording is
preserved. exclusion_manifest_lint now clean (exit 0); .438 will activate. .437 capstone
landed clean (sk48 L2 banked, reproducible_total_levels=65).

